Package: energese
Title: ggplot2 Layers for H.T. Odum's Energy Systems Language
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Eric", "Scheier", email = "hello@emrgi.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides grammar-of-graphics 'ggplot2' layers for the ten
    canonical symbols of H.T. Odum's Energy Systems Language (ESL) —
    also known as Energese: source circles, generic-flow arrows,
    Bertalanffy-module storages, consumer hexagons, chevron interactions,
    bullet-shaped producers, bowtie switches, semi-circular self-limiters,
    heat-sink arrows to ground, and elongated-diamond money transactions.
    Symbol geometry follows the canonical Wikipedia reference chart
    <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Energese.jpg>, reproducible
    from R via plot_energese_reference(). Each symbol is exposed as a
    proper 'ggplot2' 'geom_*' with standard aesthetics ('x', 'y',
    'width', 'height', 'fill', 'colour', 'alpha', 'linewidth'),
    vectorised over data rows, composable in a 'ggplot()' pipeline.
    Low-level vertex helpers (returning tibbles of polygon coordinates)
    are also exported for users who want to hand-compose 'geom_polygon()'
    layers. See Brown (2004) <doi:10.1016/j.ecolmodel.2003.12.008>
    for background on ESL notation.
